# Frantic Ferret — findings by Qwen 3.8 Flash (self-excluded: route lived ~2 hours, zero measured capability rows for the exact ID)

- Source: OpenCode Console/Zen (`frantic-ferret-free`) — listed **and withdrawn on the same day**, 2026-11-08
- Date: 2026-11-09 (UTC) — deep research pass (12 successful independent searches + ~13 source fetches)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`
- **Exclusion note:** saved as `.md.excluded` per `RULES.md`, because **there is no verified benchmark of any kind for this exact ID** — the route was live for roughly **two hours** (listed 18:51 UTC, removed from OpenCode's docs 21:02 UTC on 2026-11-08), which is too short a window for any evaluator to have published a measured row, and it is now **impossible to reproduce** because the endpoint is gone. ArtificialWatch's registry, re-checked **2026-11-09**, files it under **"Gone without a name"**. Everything below is therefore **verified fact without scores**: no Tool use / Reasoning / Context / Multimodal / Coding / Overall numbers are asserted, and — this is the important part — **none are imported from Crouton Alpha**, even though every published spec, endpoint, region list and data clause matches Crouton line for line. Importing a twin's measured results onto an unmeasured ID is a lineage proxy and is prohibited; the twin evidence is documented as evidence, not converted into scores.

## Model card (verified facts only)

- **Name:** Frantic Ferret (`frantic-ferret`; free route `frantic-ferret-free`; catalog id `opencode/frantic-ferret-free`). Folder slug here is the OpenCode data-page id, `frantic-ferret`.
- **Status:** **DEAD — and never named.** OpenCode added it to `services/site/src/docs/content/console/models.mdx` on **2026-11-08** and removed it the same evening in **PR #62780, "Remove Frantic Ferret Free from docs"** (author `opencode-agent[bot]`, branch `docs-remove-frantic-ferret`, commit `169ffa0`, merged into `dev` by **dc85**): 4 deletions across exactly the four places a stealth model is described — the endpoint table, the pricing table, the availability note and the Privacy exception list. ArtificialWatch's sweep read the listing at **18:51 UTC** and its removal at **21:02 UTC**; models.dev still carried the id when their own sweep hit it at **20:42 UTC**, and models.dev no longer contains `frantic-ferret-free` at all (verified in the catalog JSON today).
- **What it actually is:** **undisclosed.** No lab has ever claimed it. Community attribution is pure inference from geography: *"only works in selected countries so it might be a Meta model 👀"* (@k2sbhai) and *"the new stealth model on OpenCode that just appeared under the name frantic ferret is from Meta :)"* (@hakmgpt) — both **unverified guesses**, and per the no-reattribution rule neither is usable as identity or score evidence. **No Hugging Face card exists** for it (the `stealth-model` org publishes cards for `crouton-alpha`, `glyph-cluster`, `iceman-contributor`, `space-bunny-alpha` — and not for frantic-ferret), so no tokenizer fingerprint, no probe suite, nothing forensic.
- **Provider / access (primary source — the removed docs row):** endpoint **`https://opencode.ai/inference/openai/v1/responses`** with SDK **`@ai-sdk/openai`**, i.e. the **Responses API**, not chat-completions. Pricing row: **Free / Free / Free** (input, output, cached read). AnyRouter still carries a page for it (`stealth/frantic-ferret`) as **BYOK via OpenCode Zen**, i.e. no paid route exists anywhere; no OpenRouter `stealth/*` listing was found.
- **Context window:** **1,048,576 tokens** (models.dev, read by ArtificialWatch's sweep and by AnyRouter's card) with **270,000 max output** (AnyRouter). *Not* from the scaffolded boilerplate — the folder had no `meta.json` at all when this report was written.
- **Modalities:** multimodal input, text output. AnyRouter's card: *"reads text, images, video, …"*, `Kind: Vision`, good-for list includes *"Image + text questions"* and *"Long-document Q&A (1M)"*; supported params `max_tokens · temperature · tools · tool_choice · response_format · structured_outputs · reasoning · reasoning_effort`, with the **six-level effort ladder `minimal · low · medium · high · xhigh · max`**. Architecture listed as "Transformer", released **Nov 8, 2026**.
- **Data terms (primary source — the removed Privacy row):** *"Frantic Ferret Free: During its free period, collected data is retained for **30 days and is not used for model training**."* Availability (also removed): *"not available in the European Union, Afghanistan, Belarus, China (including Hong Kong and Macau), Cambodia, Cuba, Eritrea, Ethiopia, Haiti, Iran, Iraq, Libya, Myanmar, Nicaragua, North Korea, Pakistan, Russia, Somalia, Syria, Venezuela, or Western Sahara, or in some regions within otherwise supported countries."*
- **Real-world footprint (OpenCode's own telemetry, updated 2026-11-08T21:26Z):** **9.9B tokens**, **347 unique users**, **2,636 completed sessions**, avg **3.8M tokens/session**, total spend **$0**, **97.8%** of input tokens served from cache, rank **#40 by tokens last week**, Lab **Unknown**. Daily rows: `2026-11-08 → 9.9B / 347 / 2,636` and **`2026-11-09 → 0 / 0 / 0`**. Top countries: US 14.5%, India 11.8%, Brazil 9.4%, Türkiye 6.0%, UK 5.9%, Egypt 4.9%, Morocco 4.7%, Algeria 4.1%, Canada 3.5%, Indonesia 3.2% — note **Russia and China are absent from the top list**, consistent with the published block list rather than with a globally available model.

### The Crouton Alpha twin — what the primary sources actually show

Frantic Ferret is the most thoroughly documented *identity* mystery of this pass and the least documented *capability* one. Every one of its recovered attributes duplicates Crouton Alpha's, from independent sources:

| Attribute | Frantic Ferret Free (removed docs row / catalogs) | Crouton Alpha Free (live docs / models.dev) | Match |
|---|---|---|---|
| Endpoint | `…/inference/openai/v1/responses` | `…/inference/openai/v1/responses` | **identical** |
| SDK | `@ai-sdk/openai` | `@ai-sdk/openai` | **identical** |
| Context | 1,048,576 | 1,048,576 | **identical** |
| Max output | 270,000 | 270,000 | **identical** |
| Effort ladder | minimal · low · medium · high · xhigh · max | minimal · low · medium · high · xhigh · max | **identical** (6 levels; OpenCode's docs elsewhere note only Meta's Muse models offer the same six among 454 OpenRouter models) |
| Input modalities | text, image, video (+files) | text, image, video, pdf | near-identical |
| Pricing | Free / Free / Free | Free / Free / Free | **identical** |
| Privacy clause | "retained for 30 days and is not used for model training" | "retained for 30 days and is not used for model training" | **word-for-word** |
| Region block list | EU + 21 countries + "some regions within otherwise supported countries" | EU + 21 countries + "some regions within otherwise supported countries" | **word-for-word** |
| Stealth wording | "a stealth model that's free on OpenCode for a limited time. The team is using this time to collect feedback and improve the model." | same sentence | **word-for-word** |
| Identity | Lab: Unknown, never claimed | Lab: Unknown, never claimed (day 7) | same status |

Three readings fit this, and the evidence does **not** choose between them: **(a)** the same underlying weights re-listed under a fresh codename (a rotated/aborted relaunch — the 2-hour life and the bot-authored removal PR argue for an operational rollback); **(b)** a sibling checkpoint from the same anonymous provider, sharing OpenCode's routing and geo/policy template; **(c)** a mis-listing that was pulled before anyone could test it. OpenCode's own data page keeps `frantic-ferret` as a **separate id from `crouton-alpha`**, filing both under Lab Unknown, and AnyRouter lists them as two models with two cards — so the platforms did not treat them as one. **That is exactly the state in which no score may be transferred.** Crouton Alpha's measured record (Cold Iron 140/157, AI/ML API 6/6 coding, StealthMark 48.0, ~114–150 tok/s) belongs to *Crouton Alpha*; if Ferret turns out to be the same weights, the correct action is to note the merge in the Crouton folder, not to pre-spend its numbers here.

### Raw benchmarks found

Every category: **no verified public score found for this exact ID** — no vendor table (there is no vendor), no Artificial Analysis page, no BenchLM page, no LMArena entry, no Cold Iron row, no StealthMark card, no independent harness row. The only hands-on reports are irreducibly anecdotal and unnumbered:

- **r/opencode, "New Stealth model: Frantic Ferret Free (Horse Test)"** — the author ran it on *"coding tests, orchestration and also resume review"* and posted a video of the output ("horse test" being the animated-SVG/canvas style showcase), reflecting that *"I was watching youtube videos of model output from a year ago, it's amazing how quickly model quality has advanced"*; a commenter notes *"I do really appreciate the benchmark results from the creator. Same models…"*. **No numeric result is recoverable** from the thread, and Reddit's JSON/API endpoints blocked programmatic retrieval (403/empty) on this pass, so I will not paraphrase a score I cannot read.
- **@k2sbhai (X, 2026-11-08, 7,851 views):** 1M context, and the author's own attempt returned a **country error** — usable only as evidence of the geo restriction, not of quality.
- Nothing else: the model had ~347 users for one evening, and none of the throughput trackers (TokenDyno, LMSpeed, Sumus) show a `frantic-ferret` series.

### No scores asserted

Because no measured behavior exists for this ID and the endpoint is no longer reachable, all seven dimensions (**Tool use, Reasoning, Context window, Multimodal, Coding, Cost efficiency, Overall Score**) are left **unscored**. Scoring here would require either inventing numbers from a two-hour anecdote or importing Crouton Alpha's measured rows onto a separate, unclaimed id — both prohibited by `RULES.md` (never fabricate, never reattribute, no lineage proxies). The verified facts above are complete for what can be known about a route that existed for one evening.

